WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.902 --> 00:00:17.648
"Hey, "Hey, Dell."

2
00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:22.611
Patrick turned and grinned at Dell, one of the pitchers on the Central Middle School baseball team.

3
00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:26.413
Dell was long, with long arms and long legs.

4
00:00:27.014 --> 00:00:30.936
Even his face was long below long brown hair, which he wore tied back.

5
00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:36.176
Dell was an eighth-grader this year, a year older than Patrick, and he was sure to be a

6
00:00:36.276 --> 00:00:37.477
starter for the baseball team.

7
00:00:38.377 --> 00:00:42.260
Dell held up a baseball, and Patrick instantly went into his catcher's stance.

8
00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:46.944
He tucked his free hand safely behind him and lifted his mitt.

9
00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:51.228
Dell buzzed the baseball straight across the empty parking lot.

10
00:00:52.929 --> 00:00:57.152
Smack! Patrick loved the sound of the ball hitting the mitt's sweet spot.

11
00:00:57.172 --> 00:01:01.256
"You ready to play ball?"

12
00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:03.714
called Dell as Patrick slung the ball back.

13
00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:05.816
"I sure am!"

14
00:01:06.116 --> 00:01:06.716
said Patrick.

15
00:01:06.736 --> 00:01:08.878
"Have you been working on your changeup?"

16
00:01:09.619 --> 00:01:13.522
A changeup was a slow pitch, but it was thrown just like a fast one to trick the

17
00:01:13.562 --> 00:01:15.363
batter. Dell nodded.

18
00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:17.585
"Yep." "Let me see it."

19
00:01:18.426 --> 00:01:21.809
Patrick signaled the pitch by wiggling four fingers between his legs.

20
00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:25.231
Dell pulled his arm back and let the ball fly.

21
00:01:27.573 --> 00:01:30.736
It zipped toward the mitt and then seemed to float as it got nearer.

22
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.742
Smack! Patrick caught it.

23
00:01:33.762 --> 00:01:35.423
"That was perfect!"

24
00:01:36.123 --> 00:01:38.085
He stood and lobbed the ball back to Dell.

25
00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:43.689
By now the parking lot was full of Dragons players.

26
00:01:46.711 --> 00:01:51.734
Patrick waved at familiar faces as Dell trotted over to walk onto the baseball field with him.

27
00:01:52.635 --> 00:01:55.657
Energy ripped through Patrick like a vibrating guitar string.

28
00:01:55.677 --> 00:01:58.779
"Man, this is going to be a great year!"

29
00:01:59.220 --> 00:01:59.600
he thought.

30
00:02:00.424 --> 00:02:04.465
It was a warm, sunny Saturday—the very first day of baseball practice.

31
00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.626
Although it was still February, it felt like spring outside.

32
00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:13.768
Patrick dumped his equipment on the bench in the dugout and reached for the old catcher's mitt his

33
00:02:13.828 --> 00:02:17.029
brother, Daniel, had given him on the drive over to the middle school.

34
00:02:18.289 --> 00:02:21.810
The mitt's leather was soft and supple like a comfortable old shoe.

35
00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:25.911
"You should use your own mitt every day," Daniel had said.

36
00:02:25.931 --> 00:02:27.972
"But keep this one for luck."

37
00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:30.889
Patrick hoped he wouldn't need luck.

38
00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:36.691
He was in seventh grade now and ready to leave Little League behind and play middle school baseball.

39
00:02:37.972 --> 00:02:40.533
He was ready to be a Central Middle School Dragon.

40
00:02:42.473 --> 00:02:45.895
A stocky kid with curly black hair hopped out of a red pickup.

41
00:02:48.016 --> 00:02:52.978
He looked around uncertainly for a second and then hauled a canvas bag out of the back of

42
00:02:52.998 --> 00:02:53.418
the truck.

43
00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:56.739
Patrick nudged Dell.

44
00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:58.380
"Who's the new kid?"

45
00:02:58.968 --> 00:02:59.628
Dell shrugged.

46
00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:01.149
"Haven't seen him before."

47
00:03:01.169 --> 00:03:07.753
"He just moved into my neighborhood," said Todd, a big and bulky pinch hitter who also played left

48
00:03:07.773 --> 00:03:10.594
field. "You'll see him at school on Monday.

49
00:03:11.095 --> 00:03:12.015
He's in eighth grade.

50
00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:13.576
Seems like a nice guy."

51
00:03:14.576 --> 00:03:15.217
Dell grinned.

52
00:03:15.237 --> 00:03:17.218
"Yeah, but can he play?"

53
00:03:18.518 --> 00:03:19.219
Todd shrugged.

54
00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:21.100
"Coach let him join the team.

55
00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.441
He must be pretty good."

56
00:03:22.461 --> 00:03:25.322
"I hope so," said Patrick.

57
00:03:26.002 --> 00:03:28.564
He wanted the team to make it to the championship this year.

58
00:03:29.728 --> 00:03:31.789
"Practice starts in three minutes, boys!"

59
00:03:32.169 --> 00:03:32.849
barked Coach.

60
00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:38.012
Patrick buckled on his shin guards and chest protector and then picked up his mask.

61
00:03:39.472 --> 00:03:43.314
Daniel, who was volunteering as an assistant coach, was already at home plate.

62
00:03:43.894 --> 00:03:47.176
Patrick wasn't sure whether having his brother here was good or bad.

63
00:03:48.336 --> 00:03:50.937
The good thing was that Daniel was a great ballplayer.

64
00:03:51.718 --> 00:03:56.320
The bad thing was— "Yo, Daniel!"

65
00:03:56.852 --> 00:04:00.474
Just then Dell raced for the mound, waving enthusiastically at Daniel.

66
00:04:00.494 --> 00:04:03.335
"It's awesome that you're going to be coaching!"

67
00:04:04.776 --> 00:04:07.997
The bad thing was that everyone still remembered Daniel Deboe.

68
00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:12.399
The Dragons had won the championship both years that Daniel caught for the team.

69
00:04:13.179 --> 00:04:16.261
Now he was in high school, but he had become a living legend.

70
00:04:17.181 --> 00:04:20.082
"Warm up, guys," yelled Daniel, smacking his gum.

71
00:04:20.983 --> 00:04:23.504
As he strutted toward Coach, he grinned at Patrick.

72
00:04:26.304 --> 00:04:28.525
"Maybe I'll put in a good word for you as starter."

73
00:04:29.325 --> 00:04:31.445
Patrick straightened his shoulders and grinned back.

74
00:04:31.465 --> 00:04:34.046
"Don't need praise when you got plays!"

75
00:04:34.066 --> 00:04:36.227
"That's right, little bro.

76
00:04:36.707 --> 00:04:38.927
Don't worry, you'll fit right into the team."

77
00:04:40.328 --> 00:04:42.789
Patrick wasn't really worried about belonging on the team.

78
00:04:43.509 --> 00:04:46.430
He already knew a lot of the other kids from playing Little League.

79
00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.571
Plus, because of Daniel, he knew some older players too.

80
00:04:51.251 --> 00:04:55.232
The only hard part of playing a middle school sport was keeping up with his classwork.

81
00:04:56.268 --> 00:04:58.870
He'd struggled with math since the beginning of the year.

82
00:05:00.071 --> 00:05:04.914
Daniel pushed the front of his hair back; a similar thick blond curl hung on Patrick's forehead.

83
00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:08.336
"Just don't get your hopes up," Daniel went on.

84
00:05:08.356 --> 00:05:11.959
"Coach hardly ever starts seventh- graders at the beginning of the season."

85
00:05:12.759 --> 00:05:15.461
"You made starter for the first game," Patrick pointed out.

86
00:05:16.642 --> 00:05:17.442
Daniel shrugged.

87
00:05:18.563 --> 00:05:19.804
Patrick knew that shrug.

88
00:05:20.665 --> 00:05:22.726
It meant, "But I'm really good."

89
00:05:23.426 --> 00:05:25.468
Which might have been bragging, but it was true.

90
00:05:26.732 --> 00:05:30.433
Daniel had short, heavy legs that rested naturally in the catcher's crouch.

91
00:05:30.933 --> 00:05:31.593
Good balance.

92
00:05:32.854 --> 00:05:34.814
A long reach and a quick, hard throw.

93
00:05:35.394 --> 00:05:39.296
And he read the game of baseball like a champion chess player read the chessboard.

94
00:05:39.996 --> 00:05:41.696
Daniel was built to be a catcher.

95
00:05:41.716 --> 00:05:47.898
"I don't want to play in Daniel's shadow," Patrick thought as he watched Daniel consulting with Coach about

96
00:05:47.918 --> 00:05:48.498
a few things.

97
00:05:49.859 --> 00:05:52.979
Patrick was shorter and lighter than his brother but just as quick.

98
00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.640
And he worked hard.

99
00:05:55.596 --> 00:05:58.117
He slipped his hand in his mitt and flexed his fingers.

100
00:05:58.878 --> 00:06:02.460
This was the year to make his own mark on Dragons baseball history.

101
00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.381
It was his turn to catch for the team.

102
00:06:06.682 --> 00:06:09.844
The new kid from the red truck dumped his bag next to Patrick's.

103
00:06:11.805 --> 00:06:12.665
"Hey. I'm Patrick."

104
00:06:12.685 --> 00:06:16.167
"Mickey. My family just moved here.

105
00:06:16.747 --> 00:06:17.828
Patrick Deboe, right?

106
00:06:18.328 --> 00:06:19.409
I've heard you're pretty good."

107
00:06:20.469 --> 00:06:21.990
Patrick shrugged.

108
00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:23.091
"I've been playing awhile."

109
00:06:23.111 --> 00:06:24.932
"Me too."

110
00:06:25.288 --> 00:06:25.948
Mickey grinned.

111
00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.549
"Started playing T-ball and kept going.

112
00:06:29.029 --> 00:06:33.610
I was hoping to make starter at my old school, but my mom got transferred here before baseball

113
00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:34.371
season began."

114
00:06:34.391 --> 00:06:37.191
"That's tough," said Patrick.

115
00:06:38.852 --> 00:06:39.592
Mickey shrugged.

116
00:06:39.972 --> 00:06:41.032
"Nothing I can do about it.

117
00:06:41.693 --> 00:06:44.693
I'm lucky that Coach is letting me on the team since I missed tryouts."

118
00:06:45.634 --> 00:06:47.114
"Coach does what's best for the team.

119
00:06:47.814 --> 00:06:49.975
So you must be a good player," said Patrick.

120
00:06:51.015 --> 00:06:52.255
"I hope I don't disappoint him."

121
00:06:52.956 --> 00:06:54.256
Mickey reached into his bag.

122
00:06:56.376 --> 00:06:58.799
Patrick was about to ask what position Mickey played.

123
00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.962
Then he saw what Mickey had pulled out.

124
00:07:03.564 --> 00:07:04.425
A catcher's mitt.
